    {
      "paragraphId": "P00054",
      "path": "tabs.t.0.body.content[54]",
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "tabTitle": "Tab 1",
      "segmentId": null,
      "startIndex": 4969,
      "endIndex": 5119,
      "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "isListItem": false,
      "listId": null,
      "nestingLevel": null,
      "table": null,
      "text": "1. Cold Washes Only: Always wash your cotton and linen in cold water. Hot water can break down natural fibers and fade those brilliant summer colors.",
      "protectedControls": []
    },
    {
      "paragraphId": "P00055",
      "path": "tabs.t.0.body.content[55]",
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "tabTitle": "Tab 1",
      "segmentId": null,
      "startIndex": 5119,
      "endIndex": 5295,
      "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "isListItem": false,
      "listId": null,
      "nestingLevel": null,
      "table": null,
      "text": "2. Inside Out: Turn your shirts and trousers inside out before tossing them in the machine. It protects the fabric's face and keeps the buttons from chipping against the drum.",
      "protectedControls": []
    },
    {
      "paragraphId": "P00056",
      "path": "tabs.t.0.body.content[56]",
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "tabTitle": "Tab 1",
      "segmentId": null,
      "startIndex": 5295,
      "endIndex": 5466,
      "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "isListItem": false,
      "listId": null,
      "nestingLevel": null,
      "table": null,
      "text": "3. Avoid the Dryer: High heat is the enemy of a great fit. It ruins elastane and shrinks cotton. Always air dry your weekend wear on a line or a good hanger in the shade.",
      "protectedControls": []
    },
    {
      "paragraphId": "P00057",
      "path": "tabs.t.0.body.content[57]",
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "tabTitle": "Tab 1",
      "segmentId": null,
      "startIndex": 5466,
      "endIndex": 5663,
      "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "isListItem": false,
      "listId": null,
      "nestingLevel": null,
      "table": null,
      "text": "4. Embrace the Steam: For linen shirts, don't worry about getting a perfectly crisp press. Just run a steamer over the fabric to drop the heavy wrinkles, and let the natural texture shine through.",
      "protectedControls": []
    },
